+// RRV RR5 extension (fukami#2, 2026-10-11): depth-of-field blur that keeps its
+// native size at an internal scale above 1. RR5 blurs by framebuffer feedback
+// through a scratch target (FBP 210 = block 0x1a40): a forward pass copies the
+// frame into it with a half-texel bilinear average, a return pass blends it back
+// with a half-texel bilinear average the other way. At scale N both targets are
+// N times larger and each resample is a 2-tap average of HOST texels, so the blur
+// is 1/N as wide on screen. With `scratch_block` non-zero (and the scale above
+// 1), a draw that matches the pattern in GSRendererHW::Draw() (1:1 same-width
+// 32-bit copy of 32x16 sprites into / out of that block, UV = XY + 1 texel
+// forward and + 0 return, the return blending Cs with Cd by Ad) is drawn from a
+// box-downsampled native-size copy of its source (PCSX2's m_downscale_source
+// path: the forward from the frame, the return from the scratch target as the
+// forward draws left it) and both passes align their texture coordinates to
+// half a NATIVE pixel (forward samples that copy at c + 0.5, return at c - 0.5
+// for a host pixel centre c in native pixels), so each round trip is the native
+// [1 2 1] / 4 kernel at every scale. 0 (the default) = stock.
+// The counts are monotonic totals of matched draws (pass 1 forward, 2 return).
+void GSRrvSetNativeBlurCopy(u32 scratch_block);
+u32 GSRrvNativeBlurCopyBlock();
+u64 GSRrvGetNativeBlurCopyCount(u32 pass);
 // RRV Gate-6 extension: when set, UserHacks_RewriteLargeST also collapses
 // every triangle whose ST it had to rewrite (degenerate Q), so it draws nothing.
 void GSRrvSetDropLargeSTTriangles(bool drop);
