 {
+	// RRV native-size blur copy (see Draw(), GSRrvSetNativeBlurCopy). Both passes
+	// are drawn from a box-downsampled NATIVE-size copy of their source (the
+	// forward from the frame, the return from the scratch target) and sample it at
+	// a host pixel's centre c (in native pixels) moved by half a native pixel: the
+	// stock mapping sends GS coordinate p to the first host pixel of native pixel
+	// p, so a sample at p + off lands off a host texel centre; subtracting
+	// (0.5 - 0.5 / N) texels (8 - 8 / N in the 1/16 texel UV units) from the UV of
+	// a forward draw (off = +1) and of a return draw (off = 0) gives samples at
+	// c + 0.5 (forward: scratch = bilinear(S, c + 0.5), S = native copy of the
+	// frame) and c - 0.5 (return: frame = bilinear(T, c - 0.5) blended by Ad, T =
+	// native copy of the scratch target). The two shifts cancel (no drift) and a
+	// round trip is the native [1 2 1] / 4 kernel. (Measured 2026-10-11 on
+	// a0408bf, where only the forward was a native copy: the return sampled the
+	// N-times scratch at c - 0.5, which for even N is exactly a host texel centre,
+	// so it only shifted back, the frame got bilinear(S, c) and a round trip was
+	// not [1 2 1] / 4.)
+	if (m_rrv_blur_pass != 0)
+	{
+		const float o = 8.0f - 8.0f / GetUpscaleMultiplier();
+		return GSVector4(o, o, 0.0f, 0.0f);
+	}
