+	// native width at an internal scale above 1. The guest (FUN_00240cb0
+	// -> FUN_00240a48, called from func_233240 via FUN_00240ca0; also FUN_002429d0
+	// and FUN_002aaa60) blurs by feedback through FBP 210 (block 0x1a40), 1 to 5
+	// round trips per field (5 on the memory-card save screen via FUN_002aaa60,
+	// script-driven counts via FUN_002429d0, 3 in the attract) of 280 sprites of
+	// 32x16 (FST, TEX1 linear, CLAMP, CT32, FBW 10). Seen firing (2026-10-11, the
+	// RRV_PCSX2_GS_FULL_DOF_LOG log): the attract (fields 378-3286), the
+	// "SELECT SAVE FILE / Now saving" screen (1471-1537) and the pre-race fly-by
+	// (2984-3153, 3308-3704); not reached: the replay camera (FUN_002413d8) and the
+	// VS-menu caller; nothing in other menus, car select, the race or pause.
+	//   forward: FRAME = block, TEX0 = the frame, UV = XY + 1.0 texel (U0 = 16),
+	//            no blend: a half-texel 2x2 average;
+	//   return:  FRAME = the frame, TEX0 = block, UV = XY + 0, ABE with
+	//            A=Cs B=Cd C=Ad D=Cd (weighted by a depth-built destination-alpha
+	//            mask): the average the other way.
+	// Per round trip a [1 2 1] / 4 kernel in native pixels. At scale N both targets
+	// are N times larger and every resample is a 2-tap bilinear of HOST texels, so
+	// the blur is 1/N as wide (measured on field 1140: background detail 1.44x and
